        "For rods of equal original length, compare their stiffnesses using k = EA / L.",
        "The new rod has twice E but one third A, so decide how its compression for a given force compares with the original before drawing the line."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "For a rod obeying Hooke's law, k = EA / L. The new stiffness is k_new = (2E)(A/3) / L = (2/3)k_original.",
